---

## Prerequisites

Lament is engineered to run natively on the **Bun** JavaScript runtime for high throughput and rapid startup.

- **Bun** 1.0+ (Required)
- **Git**
- **FFmpeg** (Required for audio processing in `lament-scrapper`)

## Ecosystem Repositories

The Lament project is split across separate specialized repositories under the [lamentfm](https://github.com/lamentfm) organization:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/lamentfm/lament.git          # SvelteKit Web Client
git clone https://github.com/lamentfm/lament-api.git      # Closed Hono Edge REST API
git clone https://github.com/lamentfm/lament-scrapper.git # Audio Scraper & HLS Processor
git clone https://github.com/lamentfm/lament-docs.git     # SvelteKit Documentation App
```

## Install Dependencies

Run `bun install` inside each repository root:

### Frontend Client (`lament`)

```bash
cd lament
bun install
```

### API Server (`lament-api`)

```bash
cd lament-api
bun install
```

### Scraper Pipeline (`lament-scrapper`)

```bash
cd lament-scrapper
bun install
```

### Documentation App (`lament-docs`)

```bash
cd lament-docs
bun install
```

## Start Development Servers

Each service runs independently with hot-reloading via Bun:

```bash
# SvelteKit Web Client
cd lament && bun run dev

# Hono Edge API
cd lament-api && bun run dev

# Documentation Site
cd lament-docs && bun run dev
```

See [Local Development](/docs/getting-started/local-development) for environment variable configurations.
